    "preview_note": "Wolfspeed reports Q4 FY26 results with investors focused on the operational turnaround following its Chapter 11 restructuring and debt refinancing. Key focal points include Mohawk Valley 200mm fab ramp cadence, Durham materials yield progression, and initial traction of the AI datacenter TOLT and 10kV MOSFET platforms. With liquidity at ~$1.2B and annualized cash interest reduced by ~$62M, the print reaction will hinge on Q1 FY27 revenue guidance and visibility into gross margin inflection.",
    "reasoning": "Q4 FY26 revenue is estimated at $152M (slightly above the $150M midpoint of guidance range $140M-$160M) driven by resilient AI datacenter demand offsetting sluggish EV end-market absorption. GAAP gross margin remains negative at -23.7% (-$36M gross profit) reflecting underutilization charges during the 200mm transition. Operating expenses remain flat sequentially at $71M, leading to an operating loss of -$107M. Interest expense steps down to $36.5M post-March refinancing, resulting in net loss of -$145M (diluted EPS of -$2.99) and adjusted EPS of -$2.31. Free cash flow burn improves to -$113M as net CapEx moderates."
